## Rules

- Pick the slug whose description best matches the fact. Judge by the fact's subject matter, not by surface words.
- Each fact gets exactly one slug. If none clearly fits, use `misc`.
- Do not invent new slugs. Use only the slugs listed above, verbatim.
- Label every fact in the input. Preserve the input order and indices.

